meta {
  name: 24-See my inspections (attempted)
  type: http
  seq: 24
}

get {
  url: {{host}}/api/inspections/mine
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{temi_token}}
}

assert {
  res.status: in [200, 401, 404]
}

docs {
  Where can I see my upcoming inspection? I want a "my bookings"
  page like Booking.com. The spec only documents POST /inspections
  — there's no GET /inspections/mine, no GET /inspections/{id}, no
  way to read what I just submitted, no way to cancel. The
  persona doc explicitly says "I can cancel before the slot time?
  (confirm — may not be in current scope)" — and the spec
  confirms: NO, you can't.

  Trying anyway — expecting 404.
}
